    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The diagonal core shared by the liar sentence, Russell's paradox and the barber -- each of them constructs an object whose defining property forces exactly this equivalence, and each is refuted by this one line. It is included because it is the ONLY member of that family our fragment can actually decide: the set-theoretic and arithmetic versions need comprehension or self-reference machinery we have no term for. See F:barber-no-such-barber for the first-order dressing, which we can state but not certify, and F:godel-first-incompleteness for the arithmetic one, which we cannot state at all.\n\nOn the axiom footprint: it names the trust base of the SMT ROUTE that established this fact -- the axeyum-ir Boolean evaluator, and the two-valued semantics of the SMT-LIB Bool sort that makes exhaustive truth-table enumeration a proof. It is deliberately NOT empty and deliberately NOT a Lean axiom list. Nothing here went through axeyum's Lean kernel. Measured 2026-08-14 with `cargo run -q -p axeyum-lean-kernel --example nat_axiom_inventory`: the `logic` prelude reports axiom=0 opaque=0 quotient=0, and its declarations are exactly True, False, And, Or, Iff, Not (as `a -> False`), Eq and Exists -- an intuitionistic core with no `Classical.em`, no `propext` and no `Quot.sound`. Zero trusted declarations there means the kernel assumes nothing, not that it can prove everything.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
